  "modelingNotes": [
    "Shared kit for the Golden Gate Park models (sf-de-young, sf-cal-academy, sf-conservatory-of-flowers, sf-spreckels-temple-of-music, sf-dutch-windmill). The de Young's own geometry is further down, under `import.meta.main`, so importing the kit builds nothing.",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"sf-de-young\", model \"sf-de-young\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/c3921f733df14b41e1f6d15853cce7b343886f17/generators/sf-de-young.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches.",
    "Window panels clipped to the walls behind them; 346 m² of glazing with no wall behind it (curtain walls, glazing past a wall's edge) uses the sf-de-young-glazing finish in the window colour."
  ],
